>> title: Lentil Soup
>> servings: 6
>> source: https://www.recipetineats.com/lentil-soup/#wprm-recipe-container-20178

Heat @olive oil{2%tbsp} in a #large pot{} over medium heat. Add @garlic{2%cloves}(minced) and @onion{1}(chopped), cook for ~{2%minutes}.

Add @celery{2%ribs}(chopped) and @carrot{1}(large, chopped), cook for ~{7-10%minutes} or until softened and the onion is sweet. Don't rush this step, it is key to the flavour base of the soup.

Add all remaining ingredients except @lemon{1}(zest + juice) and @salt{}(to taste). Stir.

Increase heat and bring to simmer. Scoop scum on the surface off and discard (do this again during cooking if required). Place lid on and turn heat down to medium low. Simmer for ~{35-40%minutes} or until lentils are soft.

Remove @bay leaves{2}.

Thicken Soup: Using a stick blender, do 2 or 3 quick whizzes to thicken the soup. Or transfer about @soup{2%cups} to a #?blender{}, let it cool slightly, then hold lid with tea towel and blend then transfer back into pot.

Add a touch of water if you want to adjust soup consistency. Season to taste with @salt{} and @pepper{}(each). Grate over the zest of the @lemon{1} then add a squeeze of @lemon{1} juice just before serving. Garnish with @parsley{}(chopped) if desired and serve with @?warm bread{} to slather liberally with @?butter{}!